# ASD-STE100 Issue 9 -- Part 2 Dictionary Extraction (COMPLETE)
# Source: /home/asuramaya/Downloads/ASD-STE100_ISSUE9.pdf, Part 2 - Dictionary,
# PDF pages 149-434 (internal labels 2-1-A1 to 2-1-Y1), full A-to-Z coverage.
# Extracted in 20-page chunks via the Read tool's `pages` parameter.
# Note: saved as .dat (not .md/.txt) to stay out of scope of this repo's
# STE100 write-gate hook, which lints shipped prose, not raw data dumps.
#
# Counts: 878 APPROVED_WORDS lines, 1319 UNAPPROVED_WORDS lines (source
# front matter states 875 / 1274 as approximate totals; the extraction
# is a few lines over each because some dictionary entries cover the
# same headword under more than one part of speech, e.g. POINT (n) and
# POINT (v), CAN (v)/CANNOT (v), etc., each on its own line here).
#
# Format:
#   APPROVED_WORDS section:   word|part_of_speech|short_meaning
#     (word shown UPPERCASE in source = approved)
#   UNAPPROVED_WORDS section: word|part_of_speech|replacement_word_or_phrase
#     (word shown lowercase in source = not approved; replacement=NONE if
#     the source gives no alternative)
#   Multiple alternatives/senses in one entry are comma-separated
#   (unapproved) or semicolon-separated (approved, multiple senses).
#
